WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.875
Mastery Starter 7.0.

00:00:02.875 --> 00:00:04.880
New to On-Chain Analytics?

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:05.940
Start here.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.027
In about ten minutes, you'll go from

00:00:08.027 --> 00:00:09.720
zero to ready for this module.

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.265
Everything on a public blockchain can be

00:00:13.265 --> 00:00:15.920
seen, but not everything can be understood.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.486
On-chain analytics means reading that data carefully: who

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:22.745
moved what, where liquidity sits, how positioned the

00:00:22.745 --> 00:00:25.328
market is, without jumping to conclusions.

00:00:26.628 --> 00:00:29.623
Explorer: a site showing every transaction.

00:00:29.623 --> 00:00:32.658
Netflow: exchange inflows minus outflows.

00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:36.828
MVRV: market value ÷ realised value.

00:00:36.828 --> 00:00:40.344
Open interest: total open futures contracts.

00:00:40.344 --> 00:00:42.419
Depth: how much a trade moves price.

00:00:43.719 --> 00:00:45.354
Modules 0–6.

00:00:46.654 --> 00:00:49.835
Find your own last transaction on an explorer

00:00:49.835 --> 00:00:53.569
and identify: status, fee, method and token transfers.

00:00:54.869 --> 00:00:58.646
Beginner: Reads transactions and addresses on explorers.

00:00:58.646 --> 00:01:01.579
Practitioner: Uses flows, holder, activity

00:01:01.579 --> 00:01:04.266
and liquidity metrics with caveats.

00:01:04.266 --> 00:01:07.920
Master: Combines on-chain, derivatives and liquidity data

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.881
into a research view without over-interpreting.

00:01:12.182 --> 00:01:15.362
You've mastered this module when every metric in your

00:01:15.362 --> 00:01:18.247
research has a definition, a source and a caveat.

00:01:19.547 --> 00:01:22.062
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:01:22.062 --> 00:01:26.042
Next up, Lesson 7.1: On-chain data foundations.
